<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Bougainville says future still unclear.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Bougainville says future still unclear.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bougainville Copper Ltd on Tuesday posted a net profit of 5.65 million Papua New Guinea kina (US$4.12 million) based on ongoing transactions, but said little progress had been made to end the secessionist rebellion that shut its main asset, the Panguna copper mine, in May 1989.</p>
<p>The 1996 profit compares with a net profit of 7.23 million kina in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;Although the restoration of law and order and of normal conditions of life on Bougainville remain a priority for the national government, little progress has been made in 1996,&quot; Bougainville said.</p>
</text>
